      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass after these things, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the butler of the king of Egypt and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " baker had offended their lord the king of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh was wroth with two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his officers, with the chief of the butlers, and with the chief of the bakers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he put them in custody in the house of the captain of the guard, into the prison, the place where Joseph ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bound.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the captain of the guard charged Joseph with them, and he served them; and they continued a season in custody.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they dreamed a dream both of them, each man his dream in one night, each man according to the interpretation of his dream; the butler and the baker of the king of Egypt, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bound in the prison.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph came to them in the morning, and looked upon them, and behold, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he asked Pharaoh's officers that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him in the ward of his lord's house, saying, Why look ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sad to-day?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said to him, We have dreamed a dream, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no interpreter of it. And Joseph said to them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not interpretations ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "belong",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to God? tell me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I pray you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the chief butler told his dream to Joseph, and said to him, In my dream, behold, a vine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And on the vine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three branches: and it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as though it budded, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its blossoms shot forth; and its clusters brought forth ripe grapes:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh's cup ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in my hand: and I took the grapes, and pressed them into Pharaoh's cup, and I gave the cup into Pharaoh's hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph said to him, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the interpretation of it: The three branches ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three days;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet within three days shall Pharaoh lift up thy head, and restore thee to thy place: and thou shalt deliver Pharaoh's cup into his hand, after the former manner when thou wast his butler.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But think on me when it shall be well with thee, and show kindness to me, I pray thee, and make mention of me to Pharaoh, and bring me out of this house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For indeed I was stolen away from the land of the Hebrews: and here also have I done nothing that they should put me into the dungeon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the chief baker saw that the interpretation was good, he said to Joseph, I also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in my dream, and behold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three white baskets on my head:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in the uppermost basket ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of all manner of bake-meats for Pharaoh; and the birds ate them out of the basket upon my head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph answered, and said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the interpretation of it: The three baskets ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three days:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet within three days shall Pharaoh lift up thy head from off thee, and shall hang thee on a tree; and the birds shall eat thy flesh from off thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass the third day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Pharaoh's birth-day, that he made a feast to all his servants: and he lifted up the head of the chief butler and of the chief baker among his servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he restored the chief butler to his butlership again; and he gave the cup into Pharaoh's hand:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he hanged the chief baker: as Joseph had interpreted to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.40.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.40.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet the chief butler did not remember Joseph, but forgot him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
